WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:05.860
The world exists within a cube, observed by superior entities.

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:13.390
They transmitted fragments of their knowledge to random Earthlings as an experiment.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.770
It could be said they are toying with mankind.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:24.250
As a result, the subjects experienced a state similar to information overload, and disappeared.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.600
They literally vanished from this world.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:33.050
Even <i>they</i> can't explain how the subjects traversed to a parallel universe.

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.500
For real?!

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.630
There are plenty of other such experiments.

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:41.010
For instance, they monitored the movement patterns of human souls,

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:45.020
and fabricated a world after death for them to go to.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:50.020
This was to determine how mankind would react to the prospect of an afterlife.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:56.020
They have also measured the variance between thought patterns of human beings and other life forms on Earth.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:57.780
For real?

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.930
There was also an experiment which involved an entire city.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:05.290
They measured the range of human mental storage capacity,

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.920
and selected psychologically-apt individuals.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.700
The residents were involved in a battle royale.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:19.300
Their corpses were turned into zombies that wandered around the city, killing anything in sight.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.180
It's currently in a terrible state.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.800
For real...?

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.980
Ow!

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.790
It's hard to catch your signals.

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:12.170
What is the cousin's mission in this city?

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.380
I came here for the earthly reason of my parents moving away.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.880
What sort of alien contact did you have in your previous town?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:23.850
None at all.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:25.600
Earth is big, you know.

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:27.680
Not all aliens will visit Japan.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:29.480
Good point.

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:31.730
Eri...

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.150
Erio.

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:34.980
Hmm?

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.570
Why do you continue to act as if you're an alien?

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:40.070
Because I <i>am</i> an alien.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.650
That's hard to believe.

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.820
So I'm having dinner with an extraterrestrial life form?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:48.180
I thought the cousin had already grasped the fact that I am an alien.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.350
Huh?

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:54.830
I did say that, but I was being sarcastic.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:04:00.260
Why do such clairvoyant eyes have to be stuck in such a dumb face?

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:03.010
Sorry to interrupt your half-assed compliment,

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.840
but you misunderstood me.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.050
Condescension:

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:10.060
a child attempting to improve his own evaluation in accordance with Japanese virtu-

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.890
No!

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.560
You have an overactive imagination!

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.900
Not that I care.

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.190
Oh, right.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.160
Here you go.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.310
You still have bits of pizza stuck on you.

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.970
Doesn't it itch?

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.120
Why?

00:04:32.120 --> 00:04:35.120
I have no idea what you're asking.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.890
I have no intention of altering your evaluation over such acts of bribery.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.480
You're quite impressive.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:57.730
People who trust others and easily change their opinions are actually untrustworthy.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.530
What do you do during the day?

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:14.370
I am immersed in eradicating evidence of Earth's contact with extraterrestrials.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:15.830
Why do you ask?

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.830
No particular reason.

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:20.090
Fine.

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.510
First day of school, over.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:29.600
Since it was the first lesson, I didn't even need to borrow a text book.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.270
In conclusion, it was rather uneventful.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:42.230
Hey! <i>Transfer student</i>!

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:43.210
Yo!

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:50.320
That pronunciation of "transfer student" makes it sound like you're ordering me in some weird dialect.

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.910
Starting off as the mysterious type, I see.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.500
Uh...

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.580
Me? I'm Ryuuko.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.580
Mifune Ryuuko.

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.170
Niwa-kun, where do you live?

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.960
Uh... oh.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:06.470
It's where this big star symbol is.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.720
Uh... I can't get my hands free.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:11.970
Mifune-san?

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.610
Virtuous perversion.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.230
Is that an oxymoron?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.900
It's wet from her lip balm, or could it be her saliva?

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:29.490
But so what? Really, so what?

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:30.490
I'll preserve it.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:34.370
We're heading in the same direction 'til that intersection. Road buddies!

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:35.240
Road buddies!

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.620
What the hell is wrong with me?

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:39.040
Hey, want to go together?

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:40.960
Yeah!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.710
Wait, why? I mean, I don't mind.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:46.210
I don't mind at all, but- what's that?

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:47.420
Huh?

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:52.050
You'll get a booboo if you fall!

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:58.810
This is a magical item that prevents your scalp and hair from getting ripped off! Equipped!

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:01.310
Are you gonna leave your head naked?

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:05.820
"Naked" isn't ordinarily used to describe areas limited to your head.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.940
None of my friends wear one either.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:12.240
But doesn't it scare you? Cars are super fast!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.280
Bicycles are fast too.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:16.990
Well, I ride slowly.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:21.500
Really? I'm insanely fast, so I might leave you behind!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.170
I still won't go faster, though.

00:07:24.170 --> 00:07:26.250
What? Go faster!

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:28.210
All right! Let's go!

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.010
Come on, over here! Tell me more about yourself.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.970
Niwa Makoto, fail.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.140
Number of times being hit on before: 0

00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.180
Ways to refuse: None

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:37.260
Ways to resist: None

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:44.560
Niwa-kun, you're awesome!

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.480
You're so hot!

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.320
Wait up, dammit!

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.820
Stand tall.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:55.530
You may be rusty, but you're not dead yet!

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:03.000
It seems we wasted a lot of energy for nothing.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:04.500
Yeah.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:08.500
But I like these youthful moments.

00:08:08.500 --> 00:08:11.510
I'm sure this will become a great memory one day!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.260
So, this is the city.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.930
Hey, listen...

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:24.190
Actually, I don't have to wait at this intersection.

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:25.520
I live that way.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:26.770
I see.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:30.440
It's too bad we didn't have much time to talk.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.440
I agree.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:34.700
But we can continue this chat tomorrow.

00:08:37.580 --> 00:08:39.580
I guess we should go now.

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:41.450
Yes, uh...

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.960
Niwa-kun.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.580
I hope you make lots of friends!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.340
"Oh"? Whatever, oh!

00:08:56.800 --> 00:09:00.850
In order to investigate alien civilizations,

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:04.310
I shall grant you an imperative delivery mission.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:08.060
In other words, Watson, you're my assistant.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.080
Transfer student.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:22.410
Which makes you an "existing student."

00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:24.870
Yes, I'm in the eleventh grade.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.920
Uh, we're in the same grade, even the same class.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:29.920
I know.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.010
Have you heard?

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.180
Heard what?

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:46.730
I just wanted to tell you that I'm not repeating the grade.

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:52.400
I'm tall, so people assume I'm older.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:53.400
I see.

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.990
What? That wasn't funny?

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:57.910
I thought it was a good joke.

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.660
I would describe her as a giant oarfish.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:05.500
It looks beautiful at sea, but on land, reality kicks in.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.460
Her eyebrows are freakishly long!

00:10:11.340 --> 00:10:13.630
Let's munch-munch our lunch!

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:17.010
Mifune-san.

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:21.050
You can call me Ryuuko. Actually, you must!

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:22.970
Vegetarian?

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.560
Hmm... More like a <i>fruitarian</i>?

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:33.940
I want to be such a tropical girl that fruit juice runs through my veins!

00:10:34.570 --> 00:10:37.360
Ryuushi, here's our club notes.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.570
I'm not "Ryuushi", geez!

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.580
Mikki! Apologize and say my name correctly!

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.080
Make sure you don't miss an entry, <i>Ryuushi!</i>

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.450
See you after school.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:49.920
Ryuushi-san.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.080
It's Ryuuko!

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:56.340
"Ryuushi" means "grain". "Ryuuko" is a name!

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.170
Why does she call you "Ryuushi"?

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.590
Oh, if you write my name in kanji,

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:04.220
I don't like it, but...

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.350
It reads "Ryuuko" and "Ryuushi".

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:08.060
Which one is correct?

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.230
Ryuuko, of course!

00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:13.610
There was a girl who called me that last year.

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:18.740
I corrected her, but "Ryuushi is nicer and more cosmic," she said.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.610
Before I knew it, everyone started calling me that.

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.490
The name's a hazard.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:26.370
Oh?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:29.000
That girl dropped out already, though.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Expelled, maybe?

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.830
Yeah, but they say it was voluntary.

00:11:33.830 --> 00:11:36.500
I'm sure it's complicated.

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:45.470
I have club activities today. See you tomorrow!

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:50.230
Judging from her personality, she's either in drama club or the basketball team.

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:59.610
It's like a giant swordfish is being hung by a crane.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.450
Why, if it isn't the transfer student.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.410
She's like a standing version of the girl in The Exorcist.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:16.920
Did you bike here?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.380
Are you planning to join a club?

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.800
Not really, you?

00:12:25.260 --> 00:12:29.100
All the clubs tried to recruit me this time last year,

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:33.100
but everyone shunned me the following week.

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:35.350
So I'm just an art club member who never attends meetings.

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:38.360
Would it be rude if I asked why?

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.150
Hold on.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.210
Thanks.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:56.830
Ugh, my ears are ringing and my head is buzzing.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.340
I can feel the blood rushing to my head!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:04.300
When I hold my arms above my head for ten seconds,

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:07.220
I start to get really light-headed.

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:12.520
This is why the basketball team, volleyball team, and the drama club gave up on my height advantage.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.850
What do they call people like me?

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:15.640
A weakling?

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:17.940
I guess so.

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:21.900
I got fired from a bookstore job, too.
"You're useless," they said.

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.700
A dignified, yet fragile onee-sama, sweet!

00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:27.820
No, a fragile, yet dignified onee-sama, sweet!

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:31.700
Either way, she's beyond weak.

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:35.790
That's one retro bike.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:44.970
Going home with a girl two days in a row, and with different girls, no less.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:46.720
I'm living the dream!

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.470
Huh?

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:51.810
I can't even beat a weakling?!

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:00.020
Why, you...

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:12.240
Are you alive?

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.990
Chance of survival: high.

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:15.750
Why did you do that, anyway?

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.460
An act of retaliation.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:26.300
Also, corrective action for your irrational refusal to establish peaceful contact with extraterrestrial civilizations.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:29.760
I never knew aliens showed themselves in broad daylight.

00:14:29.760 --> 00:14:37.140
Taking account of the rare display of keen observation by the cousin, we will operate after sunset tonight.

00:14:37.140 --> 00:14:39.310
What? I'm still going?

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:43.900
The cousin does not possess the capability required for the position of Watson,

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:47.900
but I have decided to make a temporary exception due to a personnel shortage.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.780
She's been spoiled by the convenience of bike transportation.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:54.030
Oh well, just this one time.

00:14:54.030 --> 00:14:57.580
I have to go out to buy things anyway.

00:14:58.330 --> 00:15:01.250
I'm curious to see just how cosmic her so-called operation can get.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.670
Okay, it's free time until sunset.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.210
Dismissed, farewell.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:13.720
This means that on the inside of her futon...

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.220
Ugh, she must look like a food processor.

00:15:22.600 --> 00:15:25.610
There, you're all clean.

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:32.110
Something about her is just so irritating.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.240
Where do you want to go?

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:41.080
Do heroes protecting the city's peace even need to have a destination?

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.370
I'll give you directions later.

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:43.500
Give me them now.

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:45.460
Leave home and turn right.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.880
Okay, we turned right.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:53.590
Transmitting telepathy...

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:58.390
Sorry, I left my phone and TV home, so I can't receive your signals.

00:15:58.390 --> 00:16:01.980
Which way next? Right or left?

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:03.350
Left side!

00:16:04.770 --> 00:16:06.020
Re-right!

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.530
I guess she wanted to say "right" in a cool way.

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:12.700
Rising fastball straight ahead!

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.780
Baseball is popular in space too.

00:16:14.780 --> 00:16:16.410
Sunny side up!

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.620
That's how you cook an egg.

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.620
Where is she taking me?

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:25.710
It's the sea.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:29.050
It's the sea!

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:36.180
It took us almost two hours, racing through the neighboring town to reach the sea at night.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:37.930
I can hear my steps on the gravel!

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:41.520
What are you doing?

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:44.140
You need to see an optometrist if you see things you shouldn't!

00:16:55.530 --> 00:16:59.790
Hey now, don't tell me you came here to commit suicide or something!

00:17:00.790 --> 00:17:02.750
Are you stupid?!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:17.510
Something about her just irritates me to no end.

00:17:19.390 --> 00:17:20.640
Hey, you crab!

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:22.680
It's dangerous to play around in a place like this.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:25.940
I float in this coordinate when I loosen up.

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:28.150
No, you were totally sinking.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.860
Your futon's filled up with water.

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:33.690
Even <i>I</i> don't know everything.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.990
Is that right?

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:39.120
Why did we come out this far?

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:42.330
I frequently come here for my investigations.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:44.290
Everything is here.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:46.750
Do you walk all the way here?

00:17:46.750 --> 00:17:49.380
No, I fly.

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:57.720
If I were to express it in your pitiful vocabulary,

00:17:57.720 --> 00:17:59.390
<i>I can fly</i>.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:04.270
I could have avoided that dangerous situation by taking flight.

00:18:10.860 --> 00:18:13.860
You call yourself an alien, but you can't even warp?

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.860
You should learn from a robotic cat from the future!

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:21.410
Transfer student. The transfer student at night.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.540
Hello, I'm the Sandwich Woman.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:29.750
It sounds like the name of a heroine from a crappy superhero show.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:32.130
What? That wasn't funny?

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.880
Yes, yes. We're going.

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:39.220
What is that?

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:43.640
A nostalgic, stifling, and troublesome mascot.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.890
Wait, that's Touwa!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.230
Oh, you know her?

00:18:50.230 --> 00:18:54.320
She's notorious. She went missing for about half a year.

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:55.360
Went missing?

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.900
She claimed to have been abducted by aliens,

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:03.370
but then she started blabbering about how she's an alien sent to observe Earth.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:07.120
She ended up dropping out of school after creeping everybody out.

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:13.210
Why are you two out here together?

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:15.050
Well, it's because we're cousins.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:19.630
Whoa. Are you serious?

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.970
And you live under the same roof?

00:19:21.970 --> 00:19:23.800
I hadn't said anything about that yet.

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:31.020
I just made that up, but man, you're really something.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.110
Wait 'til our classmates get wind of this.

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.270
Show them what you've got.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.280
Throw the class into utter chaos.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:42.280
People in the city sure are into schadenfreude, aren't they?

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:44.160
It was a joke.

00:19:44.160 --> 00:19:46.490
I won't tell anyone yet.

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:49.790
Why are you here, Maekawa-san?

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:52.670
I just went for a stroll around the neighborhood.

00:19:52.670 --> 00:19:56.380
I like watching the night sky, especially the clouds.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.300
In that outfit?

00:19:59.420 --> 00:20:02.340
I just happened to feel like it tonight.

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:05.760
I walk around in various getups on my days off.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.970
I'm using the alias "Kibonengu Deko",

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:10.730
so call me that at night.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.320
Welcome back!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.160
Would you like some too?

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.540
That's Erio's pizza.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:32.370
Don't worry, she's already asleep in her room, right?

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:34.540
We got back just now.

00:20:34.540 --> 00:20:36.540
Oh, Erio was really with you?!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:43.880
I heard that Erio went missing last year.

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:45.800
Yes, she did.

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:49.510
From my perspective, she inexplicably disappeared.

00:20:49.510 --> 00:20:52.890
Was she kidnapped or something?

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:54.390
Who knows?

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:58.020
It didn't appear to be crime-related at the time.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.900
She ran away from home, then?

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:03.030
It happened in June.

00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:06.360
My daughter, who should've returned home as usual,

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:09.990
was found floating in the November sea.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:16.290
The police attempted to trace her memory and footsteps, but they came up empty-handed.

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:21.760
At the very least, we know that Erio doesn't remember those six months.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.920
Simply put, she has amnesia.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:29.010
That's how she became obsessed with alien conspiracies?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:32.470
She's always been interested in space stuff.

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:35.440
I think she chose the enigmatic universe,

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:42.150
which she already had a vast knowledge of, as a way to escape from her fear of having no memory.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:45.530
Aliens? That's just absurd!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:47.740
Show us the proof, damn it!

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:50.780
She jumped a bicycle into the river from a bridge.

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:55.460
She tried to prove her story, but failed.

00:21:56.000 --> 00:22:00.460
She landed in the shallow part of the river, broke her leg, and got hospitalized.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:03.710
That's when she started wrapping a futon around herself.

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:05.800
You can't fly at all!

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:43.400
Having dinner with Erio in the park at night: +2

00:23:43.400 --> 00:23:46.730
Getting dragged into crazy talk in the process: -1

00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:50.450
Going home with Ryuushi-san, racing, and drinking juice: +2

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:54.490
Having lunch with Ryuushi-san, bonus for being the first time: +1

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.580
Going home with Maekawa-san: +1

00:23:56.580 --> 00:23:59.120
Going to the sea at night with Erio: +1

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:01.670
Current adolescence points total: -4

00:24:01.670 --> 00:24:04.750
Next time: A Strange Moment of a Girl Bound to the Earth.

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:08.000
Do you believe in aliens?
